fix(record): read the model selection from agentDefaultModel (4.4.5)

rawHead came back empty, which moved the fault from parsing to the call itself. The marker written
beside it said why: llm_selection_error "cannot get property agent without inject".

The plugin has no agent of its own, so child.agent throws. provider and model were therefore both
undefined, the request named no route, the service returned an empty stream, and the parser reported
"reply is not JSON" - sending three releases of diagnosis after the wrong subsystem.

The selection now comes from agentDefaultModel, injected alongside llm: a background pass has no
conversation to inherit a model from, and the default selection is exactly what running outside a
turn means. The stream is also counted, because "streamed nothing" and "streamed frames this code
cannot read" are different faults with different fixes.

Four releases to get one model call working, and the deciding information was a single error string
that only appeared when the diagnostic was placed inside the failing expression rather than beside
it. A helper that swallows its own reason for failing sends every later investigation to the wrong
place.

276 tests, coverage lines 88.8 / branches 69.9 / functions 82.2.
